\# FOLLOW-UP DEVELOPMENT PROMPT: UPDATE THE EXISTING LET'S SEE DMC MANAGEMENT SYSTEM\
\
Act as a Senior DMC Business Consultant, Enterprise Software Architect, Full-Stack Developer, Workflow Automation Engineer, and Financial Systems Specialist.\
\
We have already discussed and designed the Destination Management System (DMS) for \*\*Let's See Tour & Travels Pvt. Ltd.\*\* This is a follow-up implementation request to update the existing system with the additional business requirements below.\
\
\*\*IMPORTANT: Do not build a new application from scratch. Inspect the existing DMC project, understand its current modules, database, workflows, user roles, and implemented features. Extend the existing system without breaking or removing existing functionality.\*\*\
\
The objective is to make the system reflect the company's actual working process, particularly the coordination between Sales, Backend/Admin, Operations, and Accounts.\
\
Implement the following requirements as integrated workflows, not as isolated screens.\
\
\---\
\
\# 1. ITINERARY SHARING AND FOLLOW-UP MANAGEMENT\
\
This is one of the most important requirements for the Sales team.\
\
The Sales team creates or selects an itinerary and sends it to the client through:\
\
\- Email.\
\- WhatsApp.\
\
The system must maintain a complete record of every itinerary shared with a client.\
\
\### 1.1 Itinerary Sending\
\
When Sales sends an itinerary, record:\
\
\- Enquiry ID.\
\- Client/B2B agent details.\
\- Salesperson ID.\
\- Salesperson login ID.\
\- Itinerary ID.\
\- Itinerary version.\
\- Destination.\
\- Travel dates.\
\- Guest count.\
\- Quoted amount.\
\- Sending channel.\
\- Date and time sent.\
\- Email or WhatsApp recipient.\
\- Delivery status, where supported.\
\- Follow-up date.\
\- Current enquiry status.\
\
The system should preserve the exact itinerary version shared with the client.\
\
If Sales subsequently edits the itinerary, the previously shared version must remain available in the communication history.\
\
\### 1.2 Follow-up Through Email and WhatsApp\
\
Create a dedicated follow-up management system.\
\
The Sales team should be able to:\
\
\- Send a follow-up email.\
\- Send a WhatsApp follow-up.\
\- Schedule a follow-up.\
\- Record a phone follow-up.\
\- Add internal remarks.\
\- View previous communication.\
\- Reschedule the next follow-up.\
\- Mark the enquiry as converted, lost, or on hold.\
\
Every communication must be linked to the original Enquiry ID.\
\
\### 1.3 Configurable Follow-up Days\
\
Provide a configurable follow-up schedule.\
\
For example:\
\
\- First follow-up: 1 day after sending the itinerary.\
\- Second follow-up: 3 days after the first follow-up.\
\- Third follow-up: 5 days after the second follow-up.\
\- Additional follow-ups: Based on company-defined rules.\
\
These are example values only. The administrator or authorised manager must be able to configure the actual follow-up intervals.\
\
Provide:\
\
\- Follow-up interval configuration.\
\- Follow-up channel configuration.\
\- Maximum follow-up attempts.\
\- Working-day or calendar-day settings.\
\- Follow-up time.\
\- Quiet hours.\
\- Stop conditions.\
\- Salesperson override.\
\- Follow-up history.\
\
\### 1.4 Automatic Follow-up Email\
\
This is a required automation.\
\
If an itinerary has been sent and the enquiry has not converted within the configured follow-up period, the system should automatically send a follow-up email to the client.\
\
Example:\
\
1\. Sales sends an itinerary on Monday.\
2\. The system records the sending date.\
3\. The configured follow-up is due on Tuesday.\
4\. The system checks the current enquiry and booking status.\
5\. If the enquiry is still eligible for follow-up, it sends the configured email.\
6\. It records the email activity.\
7\. It schedules the next follow-up according to the rules.\
\
\*\*Important safeguards:\*\*\
\
\- Never send an automatic follow-up if the enquiry has already converted.\
\- Stop follow-ups when the client declines, opts out, or the enquiry is marked lost.\
\- Do not send duplicate follow-ups.\
\- Do not send an email if a valid address is unavailable.\
\- Do not send outside configured communication hours.\
\- If an email fails, record the failure and provide a retry mechanism.\
\- If a salesperson has already communicated manually, apply the configured rule for resetting or postponing the next follow-up.\
\- Maintain an audit trail of every automated action.\
\
\### 1.5 AI-Based Conversion Status Detection\
\
Add AI-assisted enquiry status detection.\
\
The system should analyse available communication history and structured business updates to help determine whether an enquiry has:\
\
\- Converted.\
\- Requested a revision.\
\- Asked for additional information.\
\- Been postponed.\
\- Been rejected.\
\- Gone inactive.\
\- Remained undecided.\
\
For example, if the client replies, "We are confirming the booking. Please share the payment details," the system may suggest a confirmation-related status.\
\
If the client says, "We are not interested anymore," the system may suggest Lost.\
\
However, AI must not silently mark an enquiry as converted based only on ambiguous email or WhatsApp language.\
\
Use this workflow:\
\
\*\*AI detects intent → Suggests status → Sales reviews or confirms → System updates the enquiry.\*\*\
\
Only allow automatic status changes for clearly defined, explicitly authorised events, such as a verified booking confirmation action within the platform.\
\
\### 1.6 Follow-up Dashboard\
\
Create a dedicated Sales follow-up dashboard showing:\
\
\- Today's follow-ups.\
\- Overdue follow-ups.\
\- Upcoming follow-ups.\
\- Itineraries sent.\
\- Awaiting client response.\
\- Revision requested.\
\- Converted enquiries.\
\- Lost enquiries.\
\- Follow-ups sent automatically.\
\- Follow-ups sent manually.\
\- Failed email or WhatsApp messages.\
\
Provide filters by salesperson, destination, date, enquiry status, and channel.\
