\# 2. CLIENT CONFIRMATION AND AUTOMATIC SYSTEM UPDATES\
\
The system must track confirmation based on actual communication and authorised user actions.\
\
When a client confirms an itinerary:\
\
1\. The salesperson records the confirmation or processes a verified confirmation response.\
2\. The enquiry status changes to Confirmation Received.\
3\. The system records the confirmation date and source.\
4\. The salesperson verifies the agreed itinerary and commercial details.\
5\. The booking moves into the advance collection and confirmation workflow.\
6\. The same enquiry and itinerary references remain linked to the resulting booking and Tour Code.\
\
If the client requests changes, the enquiry must return to the itinerary revision process rather than creating a duplicate enquiry.\
\
Maintain the complete history of:\
\
\- Original itinerary.\
\- Revised itineraries.\
\- Client responses.\
\- Confirmations.\
\- Sales remarks.\
\- Status changes.\
\
