\# 7. TRANSPORTATION MANAGEMENT: OWN VEHICLES AND EXTERNAL VENDORS\
\
Transportation sourcing must follow destination-specific business rules.\
\
\### 7.1 Northeast India\
\
For Northeast India destinations, the default transport sourcing policy is \*\*company-owned vehicles\*\*.\
\
The system should prioritise the company's own fleet.\
\
It must:\
\
\- Show available company vehicles.\
\- Check vehicle availability.\
\- Check overlapping assignments.\
\- Assign drivers.\
\- Allocate the vehicle to the Tour Code.\
\- Record internal vehicle operating costs.\
\- Maintain vehicle movement and usage records.\
\
External transportation vendors should not be selectable by default for Northeast India unless an authorised administrator or manager enables an exception.\
\
\### 7.2 Outside Northeast India\
\
For destinations outside Northeast India, external transport vendor booking should be permitted.\
\
Operations should be able to:\
\
\- Select an approved transport supplier.\
\- Select vehicle type.\
\- Request supplier availability.\
\- Record the supplier's quotation.\
\- Record agreed cost.\
\- Confirm the booking.\
\- Record advance required.\
\- Record balance payable.\
\- Upload booking confirmation.\
\- Update supplier payment status.\
\
The system must allow administrators to configure destination-wise sourcing rules rather than hardcoding destination names into the application.\
\
\### 7.3 Own Vehicle Versus Vendor Vehicle\
\
The system must distinguish:\
\
\*\*Own vehicle\*\*\
\- Internal fleet allocation.\
\- Internal operating cost.\
\- Driver assignment.\
\- No external supplier advance.\
\- No vendor payment request.\
\
\*\*External vehicle\*\*\
\- Supplier booking.\
\- Supplier confirmation.\
\- Supplier payable.\
\- Advance requirement.\
\- Balance payment.\
\- Supplier ledger.\
\
Do not treat own vehicle usage as zero cost. It must have an internal cost allocation.\
\
