\# 9. ACCOUNTS WORKFLOW: PROFORMA INVOICE, TOKEN AMOUNT AND FINAL CONFIRMATION\
\
Implement a controlled financial confirmation workflow.\
\
The Sales team can initiate the payment request, but Accounts must verify payment and provide final booking confirmation.\
\
\### Stage 1: Proforma invoice by Sales\
\
After the client agrees to the itinerary and commercial terms, Sales should be able to generate a proforma invoice for the required token or advance amount.\
\
The proforma invoice must contain:\
\
\- Enquiry ID.\
\- Client/B2B agent details.\
\- Tour Code or provisional booking reference.\
\- Itinerary reference.\
\- Package details.\
\- Total agreed selling price.\
\- Token amount payable.\
\- Payment due date.\
\- Payment instructions.\
\- Applicable GST.\
\- Terms and conditions.\
\
Use the configured company document numbering system.\
\
\### Stage 2: Client payment\
\
The client pays the token amount.\
\
Sales may upload payment proof or record the payment information.\
\
However, uploading a screenshot or entering a transaction reference must not automatically mark the payment as received.\
\
\### Stage 3: Accounts verification\
\
Accounts must receive a payment verification request.\
\
Accounts can:\
\
\- Verify payment against the bank statement or authorised payment gateway.\
\- Confirm payment received.\
\- Reject payment proof.\
\- Request clarification.\
\- Record the received amount.\
\- Record transaction reference.\
\- Record payment mode.\
\- Record bank account.\
\- Record payment date.\
\- Record verification remarks.\
\
\### Stage 4: Sales notification\
\
Once Accounts verifies the payment, the system automatically notifies Sales.\
\
Sales should see:\
\
\- Payment verified.\
\- Amount received.\
\- Remaining amount.\
\- Verification date.\
\- Accounts remarks.\
\
\### Stage 5: Final booking confirmation\
\
Accounts has the authority to provide the financial confirmation required for final booking confirmation.\
\
The final confirmation workflow must be:\
\
Client confirms → Sales creates proforma invoice → Client makes payment → Accounts verifies payment → System updates payment status → Sales and Operations are notified → Final booking confirmation is recorded.\
\
If an approved credit arrangement or authorised exception exists, allow an alternative approval path.\
\
\### Important rules\
\
\- Sales cannot mark a payment as verified.\
\- Operations cannot mark a payment as verified.\
\- Only authorised Accounts users can verify financial receipts.\
\- A payment proof upload is not the same as an actual bank receipt.\
\- A booking must not be marked financially confirmed without the required approval.\
\- Every status change must be recorded in the audit log.\
\
