\# 19. END-TO-END TESTING SCENARIOS\
\
Before completing implementation, test these exact workflows.\
\
\### Test 1: Itinerary and follow-up\
\
1\. Sales creates an enquiry.\
2\. Selects an itinerary from the Backend library.\
3\. Customises it.\
4\. Sends it through email.\
5\. System schedules follow-up.\
6\. Client does not respond.\
7\. Automatic follow-up email is sent on the configured date.\
8\. Activity is visible in the enquiry timeline.\
\
\### Test 2: Client converts before follow-up\
\
1\. Itinerary is sent.\
2\. A follow-up is scheduled.\
3\. Client confirms before the follow-up date.\
4\. Sales records confirmation.\
5\. System stops all scheduled follow-ups.\
6\. No unwanted automatic email is sent.\
\
\### Test 3: Itinerary revision\
\
1\. Sales selects an existing itinerary.\
2\. Changes sightseeing.\
3\. Saves a new version.\
4\. Sends the revised itinerary.\
5\. Original version remains available.\
6\. Costing impact is reviewed where applicable.\
\
\### Test 4: Backend itinerary update\
\
1\. Backend uploads a new itinerary.\
2\. Adds destination and package information.\
3\. Publishes it to the Sales library.\
4\. Sales can search and select it.\
5\. Existing confirmed tours remain unchanged.\
\
\### Test 5: Northeast own transport\
\
1\. Sales selects a Northeast package.\
2\. Transport is required.\
3\. Operations sees company-owned vehicle options.\
4\. Operations assigns an available vehicle.\
5\. Internal vehicle cost is recorded.\
6\. No external supplier advance is created.\
\
\### Test 6: Outside Northeast vendor transport\
\
1\. Operations selects an external transport vendor.\
2\. Records agreed cost.\
3\. Confirms the booking.\
4\. Supplier payable is created.\
5\. Accounts receives the payment request.\
\
\### Test 7: Accounts verification\
\
1\. Sales generates a proforma invoice.\
2\. Client pays the token amount.\
3\. Sales uploads payment proof.\
4\. Accounts receives a verification request.\
5\. Accounts verifies the bank receipt.\
6\. Sales receives a notification.\
7\. Booking status updates.\
8\. Final financial confirmation is recorded.\
\
\### Test 8: Destination operations handover\
\
1\. Sales completes booking information.\
2\. Submits handover.\
3\. System routes it to the appropriate destination team.\
4\. Operations accepts.\
5\. Operations updates hotel and transport bookings.\
6\. Sales sees all updates.\
\
\### Test 9: Internal communication\
\
1\. Sales sends arrival information against the Tour Code.\
2\. Operations receives a notification.\
3\. Operations replies with the pickup arrangement.\
4\. Sales sees the response.\
5\. The communication remains in the Tour Code timeline.\
\
\### Test 10: ID-wise sales report\
\
1\. Salesperson logs in.\
2\. Downloads their own sales report.\
3\. Report includes their employee ID and login ID.\
4\. Sales Manager views team-wise reports.\
5\. Management views authorised organisation-wide reports.\
