\# 20. IMPLEMENTATION RULES\
\
Before coding:\
\
1\. Inspect the current repository.\
2\. Identify which of these requirements already exist.\
3\. Identify incomplete or non-functional workflows.\
4\. Review current user roles and permission logic.\
5\. Review existing database relationships.\
6\. Identify existing email, WhatsApp, and notification integrations.\
7\. Prepare an implementation impact analysis.\
8\. Prepare the database migration plan.\
9\. Identify potential conflicts with existing business logic.\
\
Then implement the updates incrementally.\
\
Do not:\
\
\- Rebuild the entire application unnecessarily.\
\- Break the existing CRM or itinerary modules.\
\- Replace the existing Tour Code architecture.\
\- Duplicate existing tables or functionality.\
\- Hardcode follow-up days.\
\- Allow Sales to verify Accounts payments.\
\- Allow Operations to edit financial rates without approval.\
\- Create duplicate bookings from repeated notifications.\
\- Send follow-ups after conversion.\
\- Change confirmed itinerary versions when master data changes.\
\- Treat uploaded payment proof as verified payment.\
\- Treat AI-generated conversion intent as an actual confirmed booking.\
\
Run frontend builds, backend tests, database migration validation, and end-to-end workflow tests.\
\
Provide complete code changes with exact file paths in code comments if showing code. Explain the changes in simple language.\
\
